# Cloudflare Pages response headers: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# A request that matches several rules gets the headers of all of them, and a
# header set twice has its values joined with a comma. So the catch-all rule
# below must never set Cache-Control: it would be joined to the long-lived
# value of the static asset rules.
#
# Expo export names every file under /_expo/static/ and /assets/ with a hash of
# its content, so a given URL never changes and can be cached for a year.
#
# HTML is left on the Pages default, `Cache-Control: public, max-age=0,
# must-revalidate` with an ETag, so the browser revalidates it on every load
# and picks up a new deploy at once.
#
# No Content-Security-Policy: the exported HTML has an inline module script
# (Expo Router's hydration flag) and inline <style> blocks and style attributes
# from react-native-web, which would need 'unsafe-inline' or per-build hashes,
# and the profile screen loads league logos from third-party hosts. A policy
# could not be checked on Pages before a deploy.
#
# Permissions-Policy denies the powerful features: the web app uses none of
# them (expo-location and expo-image-picker are dependencies, but unused).

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()

/_expo/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
